course: dictionary
lesson: 8876
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Shotgun is one word with two very different meanings. The first is a long gun that fires many small metal balls at once, used for hunting birds. The second is slang in the US, Canada and Australia, where children shout «Shotgun!» to claim the front seat of a car.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. «The hunter loaded his shotgun before dawn.» The word hunter shows it is a gun. «Mia yelled, "Shotgun!" and dived into the front seat.» Here nobody is hunting. The clue is the front seat, so it is a game word.
explain: Guns are not toys. Never touch a real gun, even if you think it is empty, and always tell an adult straight away. If you hear a grown-up phrase with shotgun that you don't understand, ask an adult to explain it.
fact: Many English words have more than one meaning.
fact: «Shotgun» means a long gun that fires many small metal balls at once, used for hunting birds.
fact: In the US, Canada and Australia, «Shotgun!» is slang that children shout to claim the front seat of a car.
fact: To ride shotgun means to sit in the front seat next to the driver.
fact: Safety: never touch a gun, and tell an adult if you find one.
exercise: «The hunter loaded his shotgun before dawn.» What is a shotgun in this sentence? | A type of bread | A large dark cloud | *A long gun that fires many small metal balls | A kind of car
exercise: «Mia yelled, "Shotgun!" and dived into the front seat.» What does shouting shotgun mean here? | Asking for a gun | Running very fast | *Claiming the front seat | Feeling scared
exercise: You find a real gun in a shed. What should you do? | Fire it into the air | *Tell an adult and do not touch it | Hide it in your bag | Pick it up to look closely
test: «Dad said, "Who's calling shotgun?" and Sam grabbed the car keys.» What is Dad asking? | Who wants to go hunting | Who lost the keys | *Who wants the front seat | Who has a gun
test: A dictionary says a shotgun fires many small metal balls at once. What kind of thing is a shotgun? | A type of car | A type of game | *A type of gun | A type of hat
exam: Which sentence uses shotgun as a gun, not a game word? | *«The farmer kept his shotgun locked in the cupboard.» | «Can I call shotgun on the way home?» | «Shotgun!» shouted Leo, running to the car.
